<title>CANADA: Hollinger's Southam deal appeal date set.</title>
<headline>Hollinger's Southam deal appeal date set.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Federal Court of Appeal set April 9 as the hearing date for an appeal of Hollinger Inc's takeover of the Southam Inc newspaper company, the group that launched the challenge said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;After hearing arguments from both sides last Friday, the Federal Court agreed to expedite the appeal of an earlier ruling that rejected the Council's bid to block the merger,&quot; the Council of Canadians, a public interest group, said in a statement.</p>
<p>In December the court ruled against the Council's bid to seek legal review of the merger.</p>
<p>Some Canadians have argued that the concentration of newspaper ownership would limit the diveristy of expression.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
